Description: offline generator of Bitcoin paper wallets and BIP39 seed cards
 Two command line programs that generate Bitcoin keys and BIP39 seeds on a
 computer disconnected from the network and lay them out in a duplex A4 PDF,
 to be printed, cut and folded into a card the size of a credit card.
 .
  * paperwallet creates P2WPKH (bc1q...) addresses with their private keys,
    in clear or BIP38-encrypted, from system randomness, from user entropy
    such as dice rolls, or derived from a BIP39 seed, at the standard
    receive addresses of its account or at random paths outside it; it can
    also search for vanity address prefixes.
  * paperseed creates a BIP39 seed card with the numbered words, a SeedQR
    and the account xpub.
 .
 The private key is folded inside the card, under a random pattern that
 hides it when held against the light; outside there is only the address.
 The programs disable networking at startup and print only public data.
